WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.398
Start and controls
Take a seat and press Ready. The host starts when everyone is ready. Your cards or dice are at the bottom.

00:00:13.398 --> 00:00:19.698
Follow the turn prompt. Wait for animations to finish; an expired turn is played automatically. Use Return to room after settlement.

00:00:19.698 --> 00:00:31.697
Jungle: eight animals per side
We are red and move first. Rivers, traps and dens affect how each of the eight animals can move and fight.

00:00:31.697 --> 00:00:45.697
Goal: enter the opposing den
Entering the enemy den wins without capturing every animal. Capturing them all or leaving the opponent no legal move also wins.

00:00:45.697 --> 00:01:07.697
Select an animal, then a legal square
Ordinary moves are one orthogonal square; your own den is forbidden. Select an animal to see targets, then choose one. Touch normally requires confirmation.

00:01:07.697 --> 00:01:18.697
Only rats enter water
Our red rat is on the riverbank and can now enter the water. Legal target hints exclude water squares other animals cannot reach.

00:01:18.697 --> 00:01:27.697
Water and land animals cannot capture each other across the bank. Rats may leave onto empty land; two rats in water can capture each other.

00:01:27.697 --> 00:01:39.797
Faster play: ranks and captures
Speed up until the sides meet. From strongest down: elephant, lion, tiger, leopard, wolf, dog, cat, rat. Equal ranks can capture each other.

00:01:39.797 --> 00:01:49.697
Exception: a rat on land can capture an elephant; an elephant cannot capture a rat. Enemy traps change ranks separately.

00:01:49.697 --> 00:02:01.797
Lions and tigers leap across rivers
Speed through the approach and watch the blue lion’s long river leap, followed by the red elephant’s recapture.

00:02:01.797 --> 00:02:11.696
A leap crosses the full river in a straight line to an empty square or capturable enemy. Any rat in the crossed water blocks it.

00:02:11.696 --> 00:02:22.696
Traps weaken invading animals
Watch the next captures at higher speed. Each den’s three traps protect its defender; check them before approaching.

00:02:22.696 --> 00:02:31.695
An animal in an enemy trap has rank 0: it cannot capture and any enemy can capture it. Leaving restores its rank.

00:02:31.695 --> 00:02:43.795
Fast-forward to the den approach
Both sides keep moving and fighting as the red lion approaches the opposing den. Every action leading to the finish is included.

00:02:43.795 --> 00:02:53.695
A run of 100 plies without capture draws automatically. A draw offer on your turn requires the opponent’s agreement.

00:02:53.695 --> 00:03:07.695
The final step into the den
The red lion is now beside the blue den. Red can enter it and let the server settle the match.

00:03:07.695 --> 00:03:24.700
Result: red enters the enemy den
After 55 moves the red lion enters blue’s den. Both sides still have animals, but the match ends immediately. Review the result and return to the room.
